x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{2}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ \\\\ &= \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16185a8f-1aed-53a4-8147-fb86611335ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{a}^{4}{b}^{5}{c}^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549356} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca2d046-b650-55fd-a1d2-c96295731924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{a}^{8}{b}^{5}{c}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549372} {:answer/id #uuid "28dcf52a-fdfa-5969-9364-91741721e814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{a}^{4}{b}^{8}{c}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549402} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb267c2-4d81-510b-a0ac-9f51187c8d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{a}^{5}{b}^{4}{c}^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549594} {:answer/id #uuid "c5129a7e-e66a-5aca-be73-9cc77c8b5f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{4}{b}^{5}{c}^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16185a8f-1aed-53a4-8147-fb86611335ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{a}^{4}{b}^{5}{c}^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549356} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0743b1d-d7b4-5ff8-9fc5-8af0138bd88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "759e1619-eead-5907-8f58-8d6fbf13ba52" :question/math-academy-id "q-2648" :question/problem "If $x=\\frac{81{a}^{8}}{{b}^{2}{c}^{3}}$ and $y=\\frac{{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}},$ then $xy=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute for $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =(\\frac{81{a}^{8}}{{b}^{2}{c}^{3}})\\cdot (\\frac{{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{81{a}^{8}{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}{b}^{2}{c}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the fraction, group the three variables separately, and apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{81{a}^{8}{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}{b}^{2}{c}^{3}} &= \\frac{81}{9}\\cdot \\frac{{a}^{8}}{{a}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{{b}^{7}}{{b}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{11}}{{c}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{81}{9}\\cdot {a}^{(8-4)}\\cdot {b}^{(7-2)}\\cdot {c}^{(11-3)} \\\\ &= 9{a}^{4}{b}^{5}{c}^{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3010ad72-5935-55f4-a972-2133c2f9cacc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549420} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3af29e-c891-5b3d-91d7-0ee584444542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27{y}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549589} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4ed26e-84c6-586f-98a0-82989e8a7dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549674} {:answer/id #uuid "cc14420e-7afe-5666-ae48-76b590082c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27{y}^{3}}{{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549698} {:answer/id #uuid "e785e421-4990-562e-bcc2-6b724b6ea31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{y}^{3}}{{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc14420e-7afe-5666-ae48-76b590082c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27{y}^{3}}{{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549698} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e11030-4cbc-51ae-ad3e-605289271154" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cb24353-5541-5833-aaa7-2a27c3864cfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-424" :question/problem "${(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by using the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}^{3} &= \\frac{(3y)^{3}}{{({x}^{2})}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule in the numerator and the power rule in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3y)^{3}}{{({x}^{2})}^{3}} &= \\frac{{3}^{3}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2\\cdot 3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{27{y}^{3}}{{x}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(r+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549370} {:answer/id #uuid "21357de3-9850-5489-b2a4-8b42a3cf8c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(r-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549383} {:answer/id #uuid "443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2r+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549456} {:answer/id #uuid "81b04f59-9424-5ce4-9b14-2e06ca51be24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(r+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549556} {:answer/id #uuid "b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2r+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(r+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549370} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-2765" :question/problem "Factor the expression $4{r}^{2}+16r+16.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $4.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2}+16r+16 &= 4({r}^{2}+4r+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2}+4r+4 &= {r}^{2}+4r+{2}^{2} \\\\ &= {r}^{2}+2\\cdot 2r+{2}^{2} \\\\ &= (r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({r}^{2}+4r+4) &= 4(r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27fdf04b-368f-516d-9e0e-8cca33d47e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt[3]{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549400} {:answer/id #uuid "3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549436} {:answer/id #uuid "69a0d827-e260-5878-81a5-f3ff4aab7335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549518} {:answer/id #uuid "b93ea9d0-8b76-54b8-8b51-d66c68f7b7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549664} {:answer/id #uuid "bba12de4-ce73-58e0-91af-1d1824b8de14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549436} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9a3fd1a-2273-5c72-90b6-7e74178421d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9b9c93d-9a95-57ab-bfc8-b62b1c153ff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-63877" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\sqrt[3]{5y+1}$ at $y=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $y$ with $3$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{5y+1} &= \\sqrt[3]{5\\cdot 3+1} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{15+1} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{16} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{8\\cdot 2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{8}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} \\\\ &= 2\\sqrt[3]{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549388} {:answer/id #uuid "4b2e51f9-9a04-5a20-a5d2-ec9135740a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549467} {:answer/id #uuid "677f5fec-7b47-57ac-aa80-a11d479550ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549514} {:answer/id #uuid "8825f5d3-ef9c-51d5-9ac8-54ce1710ff19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549572} {:answer/id #uuid "f79a8362-7b0c-58c0-a434-d4d47dde22c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549388} :answer-field/id #uuid "15720162-78da-5cb1-b598-b8344581476a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe6f82c7-c73d-5fb8-9cbc-ff242831dba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-44680" :question/problem "Evaluate the polynomial $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}$ at $z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $z=2$  into the polynomial and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} &= \\frac{{2}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(2)}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ &= 1+1 \\\\ &= 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420931a7-bfe9-57fd-be28-96ee8c3e7a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550522} {:answer/id #uuid "52b2408a-7f36-5c00-b12f-5d5d12445119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550564} {:answer/id #uuid "7676748a-b3e1-574b-8bbc-7af2c704efdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550665} {:answer/id #uuid "847735f3-85e7-556f-ab13-996c4f671091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550702} {:answer/id #uuid "8a774edc-0a83-5eff-b7f3-8dd8b4849f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a774edc-0a83-5eff-b7f3-8dd8b4849f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550718} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6a43897-150e-534f-a498-9f892cf924c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f16c2b9-1c8b-50a4-93ab-bbcc2578659f" :question/math-academy-id "q-5994" :question/problem "$3{tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=$" :question/worked-solution "The angles ${30}^{∘}$ and ${45}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the  values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nAlso, note that ${tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}$ simply means $(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘})^{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘} &= 3{(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘})}^{2}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ &= 3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{2}-1 \\\\ &= 3(\\frac{3}{9})-1 \\\\ &= 1-1 \\\\ &= 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bdaf800-b113-54a1-8ae2-bf3062dae2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3})}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550634} {:answer/id #uuid "7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550676} {:answer/id #uuid "9adb5171-3077-5713-b717-2d95d30d3fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550760} {:answer/id #uuid "daa51955-ac64-5d0a-9e18-fab91aef7595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550960} {:answer/id #uuid "faddeef1-1236-5ec3-943a-ec3424761ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550676} :answer-field/id #uuid "d19fc5b9-fae1-5789-b1b0-38f6339993d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20eb9dff-e6a3-54ea-a4e3-f227327ba30b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111093" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}} &= \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ &= \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{3-2} \\\\ &= 3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18fdfa3b-ba02-571e-937c-7aa13525db34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550423} {:answer/id #uuid "8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550723} {:answer/id #uuid "a67a328f-fc73-5e16-83b9-a7b74893916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550806} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1eeb55-0e8c-536a-994c-dc2b50c74be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551039} {:answer/id #uuid "fd397035-a545-5279-b6e8-eafddd9a06ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550723} :answer-field/id #uuid "32bd77f9-d91d-5125-9cb1-16e58bc996cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2be8c3b4-39c9-5644-83d2-b15c8e4f70a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-293483" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}} &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{1(\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3})}{(\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3})} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{7-3} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "499727a0-3e5b-5bde-ab2e-9a316650fcf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550541} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc67d17-be4b-5361-a70d-ecc1ca22279a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550556} {:answer/id #uuid "860778fd-bed5-5bee-ad73-89d756a4e533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921865507