38} {:answer/id #uuid "ac98a90c-ced6-5f67-a7f0-29cf297dabc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560711} {:answer/id #uuid "beb7e7f4-faf0-5ad6-870f-155a809a5272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac98a90c-ced6-5f67-a7f0-29cf297dabc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560711} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0193b9-6155-5584-9bd2-1442c921f71c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf16f70d-fe20-5e04-9e8c-d37751162e97" :question/math-academy-id "q-340637" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=3x-4$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{7}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{7} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ \\\\ &= \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{7}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{28}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(14x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{28}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(28\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={a}_{7}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{7} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{7} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41027a8b-52ba-5683-92a3-eafe05f3ae05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561741} {:answer/id #uuid "4656ae6e-ba54-58ef-9045-3c8b22ec6431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561759} {:answer/id #uuid "47757023-cf17-574c-a434-8c9fe4c08b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561761} {:answer/id #uuid "98cd6248-dbbd-5c94-8f56-d826f45e58ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561960} {:answer/id #uuid "dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562132} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e578f61-c9a5-57f7-9d78-ad34f5963678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba7dd967-8709-5d76-b1fe-877b52dd2156" :question/math-academy-id "q-33475" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}}\\,$ given that $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "The square root of a squared quantity can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nIn our case, we can simplify the given expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}} &= \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{s}\\cdot \\frac{7}{s}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{{(\\frac{7}{s})}^{2}} \\\\ &= |\\frac{7}{s}| \\\\ &= \\frac{|7|}{|s|} \\\\ &= \\frac{7}{|s|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $s>0,$ and we know that the absolute value of any positive number is just itself, so we have $|s|=s.$ Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{|s|}=\\frac{7}{s}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9d67ae-479b-5212-a32d-ea72ac199fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\sqrt[3]{s{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562975} {:answer/id #uuid "3121334e-b5ff-5d7f-b931-c4cc6aff67e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{14st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563057} {:answer/id #uuid "44050778-0a11-5b3d-8de9-552e09f1598c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\sqrt[3]{28s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563097} {:answer/id #uuid "66a4a5e4-546c-53dd-b661-09d0f6e93243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt[3]{st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563184} {:answer/id #uuid "e708cbcb-204a-515f-a2ee-8880e52ab193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{28s{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e708cbcb-204a-515f-a2ee-8880e52ab193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{28s{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563454} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3551f7-6554-57bf-8d88-2777fb8978a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41a2ad72-53df-54b1-8f6d-95041c4754db" :question/math-academy-id "q-141851" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{4s}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{7{t}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{4s}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{7{t}^{2}} &= \\sqrt[3]{4s\\cdot 7{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt[3]{28s{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820e6076-fcaa-5c6f-b5f8-e29610fe3682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-20)(x-40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820e6076-fcaa-5c6f-b5f8-e29610fe3682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-20)(x-40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563233} :answer-field/id #uuid "56c69cd5-07d2-598b-b43c-0e186d6e3185" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "497dcd2a-064b-5508-ade6-dffd4f30752c" :question/math-academy-id "q-167220" :question/problem "The manager wants to determine the number of wooden tables the company should produce per week to make a weekly profit of $\\$4\\,800.$ The required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800=0.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be factored as $\\,$$6\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}} $)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We factor $6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800$ using the greatest common factor (GCF).\n\nComputing the GCF, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(6{x}^{2},360x,4\\,800)=6\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800 &= 6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800) &= 6({x}^{2}-60x+800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${x}^{2}-60x+800.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d5136f-8e3c-524a-ae1b-d2c7d6281429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{b}^{2}\\sqrt{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562943} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee323e3-08d6-546b-8935-72052398ce78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36a{b}^{2}\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563124} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2ab45f-3b8e-59d8-ae0d-a84bcaf91d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{b}^{2}\\sqrt{2a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563292} {:answer/id #uuid "cfba2d73-242a-5b18-a815-bc4b2611b506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6a{b}^{2}\\sqrt{11a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563401} {:answer/id #uuid "fc68b7fb-a728-5929-84b3-caef82248a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{b}^{2}\\sqrt{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a2ab45f-3b8e-59d8-ae0d-a84bcaf91d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{b}^{2}\\sqrt{2a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563292} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a8b84a5-9da7-5fc7-9d58-31f7e5a5ff16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60bf46ec-c41d-5bd2-93b6-b056ca651773" :question/math-academy-id "q-3077" :question/problem "$2\\sqrt{8a{b}^{3}}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{9b}=$" :question/worked-solution "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{8a{b}^{3}}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{9b} &= 2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{8a{b}^{3}\\cdot 9b} \\\\ &= 6\\sqrt{72a{b}^{4}} \\\\ &= 6\\sqrt{36{b}^{4}\\cdot 2a} \\\\ &= 6\\sqrt{(6{b}^{2})^{2}\\cdot 2a} \\\\ &= 6\\sqrt{(6{b}^{2})^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} \\\\ &= 6\\cdot |6{b}^{2}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} \\\\ &= 6\\cdot |6|\\cdot |{b}^{2}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} \\\\ &= 6\\cdot 6\\cdot |{b}^{2}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA squared number is always positive or zero, and the absolute value of any positive (or zero) number is itself, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot 6\\cdot |{b}^{2}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} &= 36\\cdot {b}^{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} \\\\ &= 36{b}^{2}\\sqrt{2a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563245} {:answer/id #uuid "9026f5ff-791a-5770-911f-0b0b83b85fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-3x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563268} {:answer/id #uuid "9c93eb0d-6ded-596d-b4ab-b36cd01140e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563296} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5245bd-caba-5f74-b81d-55f9a9e8ac2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563336} {:answer/id #uuid "ebcfccec-dd55-5089-ac9a-b0ae93280f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563245} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61d8497-db30-5312-b6cc-cc9f8eeed283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-4064" :question/problem "$3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}} &= 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}\\cdot x} \\\\ &= 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{x} \\\\ &= 3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} &= (3-3)\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} \\\\ &= 0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} \\\\ &= 3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d7d654-83a6-5095-8350-0c24ed3b09f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563002} {:answer/id #uuid "3f460124-51cf-5f31-ae09-245b7c4d361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563088} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c664c-f8c9-5f53-b9f0-e91c57fa6455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563151} {:answer/id #uuid "8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563263} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fc2ea4-ed54-5789-9c1b-da6da0a36fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563263} :answer-field/id #uuid "2edd54bc-8785-50e5-9005-f3528fdfbcbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29322" :question/problem "Simplify $2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} &= 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} \\\\ &= 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} \\\\ &= 2x\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} \\\\ &= 6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} &= (6x-5x)\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ &= x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20037864-692e-5bfb-9322-3b5120acbe5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}^{2}\\sqrt{10bc}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563017} {:answer/id #uuid "4d77eb1e-d305-5769-be60-4814a62a8015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}^{2}b\\sqrt{10c}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563119} {:answer/id #uuid "85b799e3-d57c-539f-acb8-811ec4f3f811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{a}^{2}\\sqrt{15bc}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563246} {:answer/id #uuid "d988c7ff-7f4c-5175-9b2b-46df6a682046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}^{4}{b}^{2}\\sqrt{5c}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563421} {:answer/id #uuid "e3bd976f-4efd-55f3-be7f-8f74b45ff7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{a}^{2}b\\sqrt{15c}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d77eb1e-d305-5769-be60-4814a62a8015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}^{2}b\\sqrt{10c}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563119} :answer-field/id #uuid "19a40071-b4ac-5acd-960c-d9a0e6445961" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd6c8038-fcc2-5fa5-ad44-54f20efc3514" :question/math-academy-id "q-141498" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{6{a}^{3}b}\\cdot \\sqrt{15abc}$ given that $a,b,c\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{a}^{3}b}\\cdot \\sqrt{15abc} &= \\sqrt{6{a}^{3}b\\cdot 15abc} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{90{a}^{4}{b}^{2}c} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{9{a}^{4}{b}^{2}\\cdot 10c} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(3{a}^{2}b)^{2}\\cdot 10c} \\\\ &= 3\\cdot |{a}^{2}|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\sqrt{10c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA squared number is always positive or zero, and the absolute value of any positive (or zero) number is itself, so we have that $|{a}^{2}|={a}^{2}$ and $|b|=b.$  Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot |{a}^{2}|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\sqrt{10c} &= 3{a}^{2}b\\sqrt{10c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2f4616-54cd-5516-be79-b77cd37a59b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562964} {:answer/id #uuid "1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563005} {:answer/id #uuid "40bbda36-b2ef-5389-b981-78447392ad16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{y}-2\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563094} {:answer/id #uuid "784a2285-292b-5a35-aaf7-7340d809529b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563211} {:answer/id #uuid "89462c96-0fb9-5051-8f94-3c90423306ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{y}-5\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563005} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8669faa-71b0-532d-ba32-5f961f40b158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce532f1b-ce31-55ab-8ca6-180ef8818c5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-29319" :question/problem "Simplify $3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y} &= (-4+2)\\sqrt{y}+(3-7)\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ &= -2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895d9ffc-006a-5e14-8d3d-a031c859cb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3v}{v+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565897} {:answer/id #uuid "8b898f83-508a-5c71-a91c-9734fa02e059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3v+1}{3v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565901} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b0a4d1-23a0-5efc-ad6b-fdcb29f179bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{v}{3v+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566000} {:answer/id #uuid "f0190a87-fbf5-57b6-9650-b6eac82f4005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{v}{v+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566073} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c019a7-2cb9-5d61-898a-4e58c10a6b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3v}{v+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c019a7-2cb9-5d61-898a-4e58c10a6b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3v}{v+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566088} :answer-field/id #uuid "88dbefa0-da08-5591-8494-05b870a9513b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7688caa9-079d-576d-afcf-e01cab97b9fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-14467" :question/problem "$\\frac{9{v}^{2}+3v}{v+9}÷(3v+1)=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{v}^{2}+3v}{v+9}÷(3v+1),\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{v}^{2}+3v}{v+9}÷(3v+1) &= \\frac{9{v}^{2}+3v}{v+9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(3v+1)} \\\\ &= \\frac{3v(3v+1)}{v+9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(3v+1)} \\\\ &= \\frac{3v\\cancel{(3v+1)}}{(v+9)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{(3v+1)}} \\\\ &= \\frac{3v}{v+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d4aa1a-69ae-5b4c-a5e7-5285bd50e819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{11}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566408} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb87bf4-b704-5e70-b4f3-5261c9ecd7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{10}{y}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566571} {:answer/id #uuid "cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{8}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566764} {:answer/id #uuid "d44100e7-af02-52ab-9908-f002db669ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{6}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566783} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe2668c-035e-5e9f-aaa8-412ae410941d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{8}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566764} :answer-field/id #uuid "30f3163e-b6a0-5c37-924e-1f4431be9678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11621803-c2eb-5773-8ffe-0f4ac7a22e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-141985" :question/problem "${x}^{2}y\\cdot {({x}^{3}y)}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot {({x}^{3}y)}^{2}={x}^{2}y\\cdot ({x}^{3})^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot ({x}^{3})^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2} &= {x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{3\\cdot 2}\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\ &= {x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{2} &= ({x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{6})\\cdot (y\\cdot {y}^{2}) \\\\ &= {x}^{2+6}\\cdot {y}^{1+2} \\\\ &= {x}^{8}\\cdot {y}^{3} \\\\ &= {x}^{8}{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c8b5761-5505-52d5-b16d-9caf40cd8a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(y+5)(y+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566541} {:answer/id #uuid "602c6570-8eef-570f-ab39-c5dfd88147f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(y+10)(y-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566545} {:answer/id #uuid "70f8bc63-9032-59d6-94c7-44731a339417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-20)(5y+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566576} {:answer/id #uuid "8e79ff6b-683b-5305-8568-90663d207d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5(y-5)(y-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566639} {:answer/id #uuid "f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(y-10)(y+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(y-10)(y+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566849} :answer-field/id #uuid "20bcd852-4da7-5c86-b1b8-f77067a480cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a0b67f9-e70a-56fd-9ed9-04486a79a002" :question/math-academy-id "q-80174" :question/problem "Factor $100+40y-5{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can factor out a $(-5)$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100+40y-5{y}^{2} & =-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${y}^{2}-8y-20$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(-20).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-20) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 20 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-10) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 10 \\\\ 4 & \\times (-5) \\\\ (-4) & \\times 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-20) & =-19 & \\times  \\\\ -1+20 & =19 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-10) & =-8 & ✓ \\\\ -2+10 & =8 & \\times  \\\\ 4+(-5) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -4+5 & =1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-8y=2y-10y$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) &= -5({y}^{2}+2y-10y-20) \\\\ &= -5(({y}^{2}+2y)+(-10y-20)) \\\\ &= -5(y(y+2)-10(y+2)) \\\\ &= -5(y-10)(y+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f452c3-9f2c-5647-b7af-c22e41c80791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12a\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566382} {:answer/id #uuid "23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{2a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566440} {:answer/id #uuid "7466ed08-97c1-557f-bae6-81e174a0f8e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\sqrt{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566582} {:answer/id #uuid "a76e354b-19c7-5276-987d-f27f82fdd8ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{12a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566691} {:answer/id #uuid "b7101c8e-c2e8-549e-861f-eeb818e4fc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{2a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566440} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b7404d-e71d-5caa-9f77-0a7e4942005f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bd15f40-e989-5300-b551-e3144c2c681f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142027" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{288a}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $288a$ as the product $144\\cdot 2a$ which contains a perfect square $(144):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{288a} &= \\sqrt{144\\cdot 2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{144\\cdot 2a} &= \\sqrt{(12)^{2}\\cdot 2a} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(12)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(12)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} &= |12|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} \\\\ &= 12\\sqrt{2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ae369e7-03ef-559a-aa47-3760043102e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569574} {:answer/id #uuid "81517240-0e51-5a86-8d5e-c2647c66bdbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4})}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569658} {:answer/id #uuid "a3bdcd31-eefc-5f61-a086-822a45ffbb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569706} {:answer/id #uuid "adb08300-f14d-5b4c-8cbe-a1895fc9e657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{y-4}-\\sqrt{y}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569715} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c11fb7-0ecf-5125-a1d2-9a9e38c42379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bdcd31-eefc-5f61-a086-822a45ffbb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569706} :answer-field/id #uuid "856fcbb2-090f-5a4c-8cd8-b5566b8435da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e5c00c2-c308-529c-a13c-5c3155546628" :question/math-academy-id "q-296023" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-4}} &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-4})(\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4})} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{(\\sqrt{y})^{2}-(\\sqrt{y-4})^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{y-(y-4)} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-4}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30188f5f-9a8c-5a2e-bb7f-17ac473dcc94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{w}+1}{{w}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569512} {:answer/id #uuid "3e17be7b-71d9-531e-9e23-2a887af86afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{{w}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569527} {:answer/id #uuid "6666040b-ee0e-5ca9-9d87-09de21f3571e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{w-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569602} {:answer/id #uuid "932371f4-fde9-55f2-b9db-f53acbb01913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{w\\sqrt{w}+1}{w-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569674} {:answer/id #uuid "b8de0369-bf9b-5b19-ad7f-8ab6818094ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{w\\sqrt{w}-1}{w-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6666040b-ee0e-5ca9-9d87-09de21f3571e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{w-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569602} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a720dff-cbbe-5a63-8f0f-44d10d647c99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25064e53-93b3-52b6-af27-2a0003a93f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-85321" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{w}-1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{w}-1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1} &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{\\sqrt{w}-1} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{(\\sqrt{w}+1)(\\sqrt{w}-1)} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{(\\sqrt{w})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{w-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040ec5ab-bcdf-5aca-99d8-720e6b5d8392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h(h+4)^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569451} {:answer/id #uuid "574ae8f2-ab3d-5f65-a5ac-bc1418674da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{h}^{4}(h-4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569569} {:answer/id #uuid "5d268b5c-01f0-51e5-95fd-adf189f6f7e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{h}^{4}(h+4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569582} {:answer/id #uuid "95c2c16a-d3fe-5fc6-bead-e655541975ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{h}^{5}(h-4)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569680} {:answer/id #uuid "ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee148d99-14db-571f-b95d-3fd724833b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569819} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a21e5e-fd27-5130-9714-620502136f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c4e4328-a65d-5ebb-a442-4282ed74de70" :question/math-academy-id "q-111940" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${h}^{5}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${h}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5} & ={h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${h}^{2}+8h+16$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16) &= {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+{4}^{2}) \\\\ &= {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+2\\cdot 4h+{4}^{2}) \\\\ &= {h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f3d87ed-6d1b-59e1-804f-6d88c18f0d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x-x\\sqrt{x-5}}{54-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569558} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d7b09-683b-594e-8b0f-376f8798f202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54x-\\sqrt{x+5}}{7+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569653} {:answer/id #uuid "9250b5d5-33a4-5499-